From ce08bc0f20e828054e3fca2c4806e2cd208e0e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 365/488] soh: name the 24 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_spot18_obj.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 24 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Spot18_Obj/z_bg_spot18_obj.c.

  * func_808B8910 -> BgSpot18Obj_ShouldSpawn
    deduced, confidence HIGH: looks this type and Link's age up in
    sSpawnByAge and returns whether the object exists, logging the malformed
    cases

  * func_808B8A5C -> BgSpot18Obj_InitScale
    deduced, confidence HIGH: applies this type's entry from sScales

  * func_808B8A98 -> BgSpot18Obj_InitDynaPoly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: registers the type's collision header as a
    dynapoly bg actor

  * func_808B8B08 -> BgSpot18Obj_InitFlags
    deduced, confidence HIGH: ORs this type's entry from sExtraFlags into
    actor.flags

  * func_808B8B38 -> BgSpot18Obj_RunCommonInit
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs every entry of sCommonInitFuncs in order,
    stopping at the first that fails

  * func_808B8BB4 -> BgSpot18Obj_InitStatue
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the statue's init: already-pushed or child
    Link goes straight to the settled state, otherwise the pushable state

  * func_808B8C90 -> BgSpot18Obj_InitSpear
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the spear's init: processes its uncull chain
    and installs the do-nothing action

  * func_808B8CC8 -> BgSpot18Obj_RunTypeInit
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs this type's entry of sTypeInitFuncs if
    there is one

  * func_808B8DC0 -> BgSpot18Obj_SetupDoNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the empty action

  * func_808B8DD0 -> BgSpot18Obj_DoNothing
    deduced, confidence HIGH: empty action

  * func_808B8DDC -> BgSpot18Obj_UpdateBgCheck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs Actor_UpdateBgCheckInfo with the statue's
    dimensions

  * func_808B8E20 -> BgSpot18Obj_StopPlayerPush
    deduced, confidence HIGH: clears the dynapoly push accumulator and the
    player's MOVING_DYNAPOLY flag

  * func_808B8E64 -> BgSpot18Obj_SetupWaitForPush
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arms the 20-frame push counter and installs
    the waiting action

  * func_808B8E7C -> BgSpot18Obj_WaitForPush
    deduced, confidence HIGH: requires 20 uninterrupted frames of the player
    pushing before the statue starts sliding

  * func_808B8EE0 -> BgSpot18Obj_SetupSlide
    deduced, confidence HIGH: zeroes the statue's rotation and velocity and
    installs the sliding action

  * func_808B8F08 -> BgSpot18Obj_Slide
    deduced, confidence HIGH: slides the statue out to 80 units from home,
    then sets its switch flag and chimes

  * func_808B9030 -> BgSpot18Obj_SetupSettled
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the settled action

  * func_808B9040 -> BgSpot18Obj_Settled
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the post-push state: only cancels any further
    player push

  * D_808B90F0 -> sSpawnByAge
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-type, per-age flag read by
    BgSpot18Obj_ShouldSpawn

  * D_808B90F4 -> sScales
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-type scale applied by
    BgSpot18Obj_InitScale

  * D_808B90FC -> sColHeaders
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-type collision header, statue and spear

  * D_808B9104 -> sExtraFlags
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-type actor flags ORed in by
    BgSpot18Obj_InitFlags, both zero as shipped

  * D_808B910C -> sCommonInitFuncs
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the four init steps every type runs, in order

  * D_808B913C -> sTypeInitFuncs
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-type init function, statue and spear

